(
Morse trainer
--------------

Building an "elbug" type morse key, with two contact points, and either a single 
lever moving between them, or two paddles, as is the modern style. The point
is creating the rythm of morse, which is what I am training my ears to recognize.

The main loop regularly checks the input pins, and generate a single dit or dah,
followed by a a single dit-length pause, before checking again. 

The speed is selectable somehow, for example after 10 dots we enter the menu?

Using a buzzer to create sound, and an LCD display to type the characters.

If the pause after the last dit or dah extends to three times a dit, it indicates a
new letter, and then we look up the previous. This is done as follows:

- when starting a new character, set some variable to 1
- generating a dit: shift left
- generating a dah: shift left and add 1

When reaching end of character delay, the value is an index into the string
below, using underscore to mean "unrecognized combination"

)

60 constant InitialTick  (length of dit in millis - 20 wpm)
variable Tick


Tick constant msDit
Tick 3 * constant msDah

5 constant PinDit
6 constant PinDah
7 constant PinBeep
13 constant PinLed

(-- 0-based string of characters --)
: Chars
	s" __ETIANMSURWDKGOHVF_L_PJBXCYZQ__54_3___2__+____16=/___(_7___8_90____________?________.____@______-___________)_____,"
;

95 constant UnknownChar (-- underline _ --)


: ShowChar (value --)
	Chars			(value str)
	swap over		(str value str)
	c@			(str value strLen)
	over <=		(str value flag)
	&1 jmp?
		(str value)
		+ 1+ c@ emit	(character)
		ret
		
	/1             (-- value out of bounds --)
		(str value)
		2drop
		UnknownChar emit
;

(-- test --)
: ShowP b10110 ShowChar ;


: Init 
	InitialTick Tick !
	
	PinDit IN Pin .setIn
	PinDah IN Pin .setIn
	PinBeep IN Pin .setOut
	PinLed IN Pin .setOut
	
	0 IN Timers .set  (-- for timing delays without input --)
;

: call? (cond addr -- )
	swap not &1 jmp?
		(-- cond true --)
		execute
		ret
	
	/1 (-- cond false --)
		drop 
;

(-- wait until timer 0 has moved a number of millis --)
: TWait (ms -- )
	/1
		0 IN Timers .get (ms elapsed)
		over >= &2 jmp?
		&1 jmp
	/2
		(-- done --)
		drop
;		

(-- play sound --)
: Play (ms --)
	msDit TWait
	
	512 PinBeep IN Pin .writeAnalog
	1 PinLed IN Pin .writeDigital
	delay
	0 PinBeep IN Pin .writeDigital
	0 PinLed IN Pin .writeDigital
	
	0 IN Timers .set   (-- count time since play --)
;

: DoDit 
	Tick Play
;
: DoDah 
	Tick 3 * Play
;

: MainLoop
	Init
	/1
		PinDit IN Pin .readDigital ' DoDit call?
		PinDah IN Pin .readDigital ' DoDah call?
		&1 jmp
;



	

